Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_wed: fix legacy WO CPU-boot fallback

MT7981 device trees can still describe the WO CPU-boot registers through
memory-region-names = "wo-boot" instead of mediatek,wo-cpuboot. The
carried syscon conversion stores ERR_PTR(-ENODEV) when the latter is
absent, then passes it to regmap_write() because wo_w32() only checks
for NULL. This panics while mt7915e probes on AX3000T.

Use the optional lookup to represent an absent phandle with NULL and
propagate genuine lookup errors, including deferred probes. Skip the
legacy boot mapping only when a valid syscon regmap is present. The
existing read/write helpers then use the mapped legacy region safely.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_wed_mcu.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_wed_mcu.c
@@ -356,16 +356,18 @@
 	const char *fw_name;
 	u32 val, boot_cr;
 	int ret, i;
 
 	mtk_wed_mcu_load_ilm(wo);
-	wo->boot_regmap = syscon_regmap_lookup_by_phandle(wo->hw->node,
-							  "mediatek,wo-cpuboot");
+	wo->boot_regmap = syscon_regmap_lookup_by_phandle_optional(
+		wo->hw->node, "mediatek,wo-cpuboot");
+	if (IS_ERR(wo->boot_regmap))
+		return PTR_ERR(wo->boot_regmap);
 
 	/* load firmware region metadata */
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(mem_region); i++) {
-		if (i == MTK_WED_WO_REGION_BOOT && !IS_ERR(wo->boot_regmap))
+		if (i == MTK_WED_WO_REGION_BOOT && wo->boot_regmap)
 			continue;
 
 		if (mem_region[i].addr)
 			continue;
 
